Description: virtual machine manager with Gunyah support
 librevm manages virtual machines on Linux, with first-class support for
 Qualcomm's Gunyah hypervisor. It provides a command line tool and a GTK4
 window, both driving the same core library.
 .
 It handles the parts of Gunyah that surprise people: the lend-only memory
 path, the static swiotlb, the branch-target landing pads modules need, and a
 serial console that survives closing the window.
 .
 crosvm is not in Debian and is not depended on. Install it separately and
 point librevm at it, or place it on PATH.
